<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fateh Singh Ahluwalia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a>–<a href="/years/1837">1837</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fateh Singh Ahluwalia was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> ruler of Kapurthala and head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahluwalia-misl">Ahluwalia misl</a> from 1801 until his death. He was a close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, exchanging turbans with him as a sign of brotherhood and fighting in his campaigns that built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. Fearing Ranjit Singh's power, he later sought British protection for his lands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fateh-singh-ahluwalia.jpg" alt="Fateh Singh Ahluwalia" width="249" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nanrhe10 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fateh_Singh_Ahluwalia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
